            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Match the switch to your generator's largest 120/240-volt outlet. An L14-30 outlet calls for a 30-amp switch, which handles up to about 7,200 watts at 240 volts. A 50-amp outlet calls for a 50-amp switch, which can use up to 12,000 watts. A larger switch on a smaller generator adds cost without adding capacity."
          }
