          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is an interlock kit as safe as a transfer switch?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A listed interlock kit installed on a compatible panel prevents backfeed just as a transfer switch does, by stopping the main breaker and the generator breaker from being on together. The difference is convenience: an interlock lets you power any circuit but requires you to manage the load at the panel yourself."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I install a manual transfer switch myself?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Unless you are a licensed electrician, no. The work happens inside your main panel, most jurisdictions require a permit and inspection, and mistakes can electrocute you or a utility worker. Manufacturers such as Generac recommend professional installation."
          }
