        <div id="sizing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. 30 Amps or 50 Amps
          </h2>

          <p>
            The amperage of the switch should match the largest 120/240-volt outlet on your generator, because that is the connection the inlet and cord will use. Most portable generators between roughly 5,000 and 9,000 running watts have a 30-amp L14-30 outlet, and a 30-amp switch suits them. At 240 volts, 30 amps works out to 7,200 watts, which is why Reliance and Generac rate their 30-amp switches for generators up to about 7,500 running watts.
          </p>

          <p>
            Larger generators often carry a 50-amp outlet, typically a 14-50 or a CS6365-style twist-lock, and these can deliver up to 12,000 watts at 240 volts. Pairing one with a 30-amp switch caps it at roughly 7,200 watts and leaves the rest unused. A 50-amp switch such as Reliance's 510C or R510A uses the generator's full capacity and adds room for 240-volt loads like a well pump.
          </p>

          <p>
            Going the other way is the more common mistake. A 50-amp switch on a 30-amp generator still works, but you pay more for the switch, the inlet and the cord without gaining anything. Size the switch to the generator you own, or to the one you will realistically buy, and check the outlet face on the generator before ordering, because the plug shape decides the cord and inlet.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are still choosing a generator, start from the loads you need to run. Our <a href="/generator-wattage-chart/">generator wattage chart</a> lists typical running and starting watts for common appliances, and <a href="/what-size-generator-do-i-need-for-my-house/">what size generator do I need</a> walks through adding them up. Our <a href="/best-portable-generator/">best portable generator</a> guide notes which models carry a 30-amp or 50-amp outlet.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
